        "text": "So first we need to redefine what Web3 is. And to redefine what Web3 is, we need to define Web1 and Web2. So Web1 was a transformation of information. You can access it everywhere. With email, website, the source of information was directly. You can have a direct access to it. On Web two, you got service and application on top of it. People could access to social network and have a direct connection people to people or service to services. Web3 is a transformation of value. And with value you have a total new definition of use cases going to come. We just touched 5 to 10% of the real use case. Cryptocurrency with financial value and NFT with ownership and digital artistic possession. Web3 is going to definitely arise in the next coming year with new use cases, and that's going to be the next focus.",
